TASK: Rework the Audit Role (auditor, audit, internal_auditor, audit_team) in our ERP.
Keep ONLY the petty cash replenishment audit from the current role. Remove everything else, then add a new read-only Store & Inventory Audit module.

═══════════════════════════════════════
PART 1 – KEEP (Petty Cash Replenishment only)
═══════════════════════════════════════
Keep these exactly as they work today:
- /finance/replenishments?tab=under_audit
- Audit Clearance / Approve (adjust approved amount, add audit observations, route to GM as pending_gm)
- Audit Reject (the whole cycle goes back to the custodian, explanation notes mandatory)
- Voucher-level actions: Reject Voucher (auto-recalculate valid sum), Request Clarification (clarification_needed + note), Restore/Approve
- Receipt scan/PDF viewing inside the voucher bundle
- Replenishment history (reconciled cycles, approved sums, rejections)
- The audit dashboard keeps only: "Replenishments Awaiting Audit Clearance", "Recent Replenishment History", and petty cash/imprest fund balances.

═══════════════════════════════════════
PART 2 – REMOVE for the audit role
═══════════════════════════════════════
Hide from the sidebar, block the routes, and enforce this on the backend/API (not just the UI) for:
- /audit/expense-receipts (receipt audit center and SMS escalation)
- /finance/expense-hub and /finance/tax-deductions (VAT/tax decisions)
- /expenses approval hub
- /receipts OCR analyzer
- Procurement pipeline cards on the dashboard
- Bank account balances and the system activity stream on the dashboard
- Payroll, attendance, and activity logs (stay locked)
Auditors must never disburse money, create PRs, or adjust stock (segregation of duties stays).

═══════════════════════════════════════
PART 3 – ADD: Store & Inventory Audit (STRICTLY READ-ONLY)
═══════════════════════════════════════
Add a new sidebar section "Store Audit" visible only to audit roles, with these pages:

3.1 Inventory Overview (/audit/inventory)
- All stores and all items: current on-hand quantity, unit, last movement date, store, project.
- Filters: store, project, item/category, date range, status.
- Flags: negative stock, dormant stock (no movement for X days), and large unexplained adjustments.

3.2 Stock Movement Ledger (/audit/stock-movements)
- Complete ledger of EVERY movement: intake, issue/usage, transfer out, transfer in, adjustment, return.
- Columns: date/time, store, item, qty in/out, balance after, reference doc (PR/slip/transfer/usage no.), performed by, approved by.
- Running balance check: highlight any row where balance doesn't reconcile.
- Export to Excel/PDF.

3.3 Daily Usage Audit (/audit/daily-usage)
- All daily material usage/issue records by site, project, date, and storekeeper.
- Compare usage vs. planned/BOQ/requested quantity and flag over-usage.
- Flag days with no usage record where there was stock movement, and duplicate or unusually large entries.

3.4 Material Transfer Audit (/audit/transfers)
- Every inter-store transfer: origin, destination, vehicle/driver, dispatched qty, received qty, dates, status.
- Flag: dispatched but not received, received qty ≠ dispatched qty (shortage/excess), in transit longer than 48h, and transfers where the stock deduction and addition don't match.

3.5 Purchase → Intake Fulfillment Check (/audit/fulfillment)  ← MOST IMPORTANT
For every Purchase Request / Material Request, compare line by line:
  Requested qty → Approved qty → Purchased qty → Received at store (intake slip) qty → Remaining qty
Status per line: Fully Fulfilled / Partially Fulfilled / Not Received / Over-received.
- Dedicated "Unfulfilled Materials" tab listing every item with remaining qty > 0: PR no., supplier, project, store, days since purchase, amount paid, and amount outstanding.
- Highlight "Paid but not received" in red.
- Each line opens a detail drawer with: the PR, the payment record, the intake slips (with photos and sequence numbers), and the transfer history.
- Flag intake slips with missing photos, missing sequence numbers, duplicate slips, or an intake date before the purchase date.

3.6 Audit Findings & Actions
- Auditor can add an Audit Observation / Query note on any flagged row (stock line, transfer, usage record, fulfillment line).
- The note creates a Finding with: status (Open / Responded / Resolved), severity, assigned person (storekeeper/procurement), due date, and an attachment.
- The assignee gets an in-app notification (SMS optional), can respond with notes and attachments, and the auditor can close the finding.
- Findings that stay open beyond the due date escalate to the GM.
- Findings dashboard: open, overdue, and resolved counts by store/project.

3.7 Audit Dashboard additions (/dashboard/audit)
Add cards: Unfulfilled Materials count and value, Paid-but-not-received count, Transfers Pending Receipt, Stock Discrepancies, Open Audit Findings.

═══════════════════════════════════════
PERMISSIONS (enforce in the DB/RLS and API)
═══════════════════════════════════════
- Auditor: SELECT on inventory, stock_movements, daily_usage, transfers, purchase/material requests, intake slips, and payments (view only, for fulfillment matching).
- Auditor: INSERT/UPDATE only on audit_findings, replenishment audit decisions, and voucher audit actions.
- NO insert/update/delete on inventory, stock movements, transfers, usage, PRs, intake, or payments.
- Hide all edit, delete, pay, and adjust buttons on these pages for audit roles.
- Log every auditor action (who, what, when) in the audit trail.

ACCEPTANCE TESTS
1. Auditor logs in and sees only petty cash replenishment plus the Store Audit section.
2. Calling any removed route or write API as an auditor returns 403.
3. A PR with 100 units purchased and 60 received appears under "Unfulfilled Materials" with 40 remaining.
4. A transfer dispatched but not received for >48h is flagged.
5. A finding raised by an auditor notifies the storekeeper, and an overdue one escalates to the GM.
6. All Store Audit pages filter correctly and export to Excel.

Implement all of it, then list the files and routes changed.